Public plans (`public/<workload>.<variant>.plan.json`, compact): the workload
`workloads/<set>/<workload>.json` planned with `capabilities/<variant>.json`. They are
the eight RUN-1 showcase shapes (1 m windows, 1 Hz, every 10 s), `mixed-03`,
`rangeheavy` and `topk__5m__1hz__60s`, plus a greedy cover of every node shape
(operator, timing, lifetime, family or measure, reduction, range kind, merge regrouping,
projection and binary-operator fields, and the children's operators) that the full
sweep produces. The full sweep plans all 206 public PromQL workloads (showcase, grid,
heldout, and the paper's mixed and range-heavy sets) with each of the four capability
files; every ClickHouse plan of it translates, and no equivalent-only one has a
substitution.
The sweep ran at #1374's last head, 7834fed4d. At main bc725bda8 every committed fixture was
regenerated and is byte-identical.

How each file was made: the workload was planned with
`planning_stages::run_stages_until(.., RunUntil::Stage2)` (with
`PlanningModels::builtin().with_deployment_capabilities(<file above>)`, or the
defaults), then Stage 3 `select_plan`, then
`installable_plan_of(plan, &workload.query_workload.entries())`, serialized
with `serde_json::to_string_pretty` (named) or `serde_json::to_string` (public).

Regenerate with `asap_planner --plan-file` once it exists; never edit these files by hand.
Edge cases are made in test code by changing one field of a loaded fixture.
